## Data Collection
Audio files were sampled using overlapping sliding windows (90% overlap, 
average 30-second duration). Tempo was extracted using a self-similarity-based 
algorithm and corrected for harmonics (common multiples detected in classical music).

## Conductor Classifications
\itemize{
  \item **HI (Historically Informed)**: Use period instruments and follow HI 
    stylistic criteria
  \item **HI influence**: May use modern instruments but follow HI performance 
    practices
  \item **Romantic**: Pre-1980s performances or those not adhering to HI criteria
}

## Key Findings
The analysis revealed that conductors systematically perform slower than 
Beethoven's metronome marks:
\itemize{
  \item HI conductors: 6(2) BPM slower on average
  \item HI-influenced: 8(2) BPM slower
  \item Romantic: 13(2) BPM slower
}

This systematic deviation suggests Beethoven may have misread his metronome 
by reading below the triangular moving weight (15mm high ≈ 12 BPM) rather 
than above it.
